description: Where PyTorch vs MLX code lives and how selection works
---
### Model backends

- Backend selection is controlled by the `--backend` CLI flag (`torch` or `mlx`).
- PyTorch modules live in [model/torch](mdc:src/simplefold/model/torch/), MLX modules in [model/mlx](mdc:src/simplefold/model/mlx/).
- During inference, config YAMLs from [configs/model/architecture](mdc:configs/model/architecture/) are instantiated. For MLX, the YAML text is modified to replace `torch` with `mlx` before instantiation (see [inference.py](mdc:src/simplefold/inference.py)).
- ESM2 is loaded via [utils/esm_utils.py](mdc:src/simplefold/utils/esm_utils.py) and mapped to MLX if needed.

